From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 19:08:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP: find MLD stations by link address in the TX status handler

When an Authentication frame is addressed to the peer link address, the
driver reports the TX status callback with the frame's destination
address, which is the peer's link address.

ap_get_sta() looks up only by sta->addr, which for an MLD is the MLD
MAC address. As a result, the lookup fails and the TX status callback
for the Authentication frame is dropped.

Fall back to ap_get_link_sta() when ap_get_sta() returns NULL so the
driver TX status is properly processed for MLD stations.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -7573,6 +7573,10 @@ static void handle_auth_cb(struct hostap
 	bool success_status;

 	sta = ap_get_sta(hapd, mgmt->da);
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	if (!sta)
+		sta = ap_get_link_sta(hapd, mgmt->da);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 	if (!sta) {
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "handle_auth_cb: STA " MACSTR
 			   " not found",
@@ -7745,6 +7749,10 @@ static void handle_assoc_cb(struct hosta
 	int new_assoc = 1;

 	sta = ap_get_sta(hapd, mgmt->da);
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	if (!sta)
+		sta = ap_get_link_sta(hapd, mgmt->da);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 	if (!sta) {
 		wpa_printf(MSG_INFO, "handle_assoc_cb: STA " MACSTR " not found",
 			   MAC2STR(mgmt->da));
